from pathlib import Path
import json,html,hashlib
from html.parser import HTMLParser
P=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
def load(n): return json.loads((P/n).read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
def esc(v): return html.escape(str(v))
data=load('INPUT.json'); results=load('RESULTS.json'); freeze=load('WINNER-FREEZE.json')
for n,h in freeze['sha256'].items(): assert hashlib.sha256((P/n).read_bytes()).hexdigest()==h
assert all(not r['estimable'] for r in results), 'Report narrative requires revision if results change'
style='body{background:#111d25;color:#e8eeee;max-width:1150px;margin:auto;padding:36px;font:17px/1.55 system-ui}h1,h2{color:#a7e3ca}a{color:#9fd2f5}.box{padding:22px;background:#263c46;border-left:5px solid #d3ad69}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:14px;margin:20px 0}td,th{padding:9px;border:1px solid #455a63;text-align:left;vertical-align:top}th{background:#253b45}summary{cursor:pointer;color:#b6e6d1}.scroll{overflow:auto}'
h=['<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>v87 · Development alignment</title><style>'+style+'</style><h1>Development alignment: not estimable</h1><p>v87 · Frozen v85 scorer applied to the v84 image inventory</p><div class="box"><b>No qualifying rule to carry forward.</b><br>Both available visual features are constant among known figures within every ring/group. After controlling for ring frequencies, neither has variation left to align. This is a support limit, not evidence that the historical tables disagree with the manuscript.</div><h2>Actual support</h2><table><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Known / 120</th><th>Unresolved</th><th>Within-group variance sum</th><th>Result</th></tr>']
for r in results: h.append(f'<tr><td>{esc(r["feature"])}</td><td>{r["known"]}</td><td>{r["unknown"]}</td><td>{r["within_block_variance_sum"]:.0f}</td><td>Not estimable</td></tr>')
h+=['</table><p>Torso coding: 1 garment visible; 0 bare torso visible. Enclosure coding: 1 enclosing vessel visible; 0 no enclosing vessel visible. Missing classifications remain missing. No sex was inferred. The raw scorer returns score 0 and adjusted p=1 for both constant responses; these are computational outputs, not informative hypothesis tests. Its index-0 placeholder is not a winning rule.</p><h2>Why the synthetic pass did not guarantee a usable manuscript test</h2><p>The synthetic qualification planted variation inside groups. The actual first-pass image inventory contains differences between groups, but no known differences within a group for either feature. The frozen test deliberately removes between-group frequencies to guard against layout confounding. It therefore removes all the available variation here. We have not relaxed that control, supplied unknown values, or changed the grouping to obtain a fit.</p><h2>Every eligible group</h2><p>Counts below expose the limitation directly. Unknown figures are retained but do not contribute an invented classification. A range across groups does not supply the within-group contrast required by this scorer.</p><div class="scroll"><table><tr><th>Folio</th><th>Group</th><th>Torso known / unknown</th><th>Garment / bare</th><th>Enclosure known / unknown</th><th>Vessel / absent</th></tr>']
b,e=results
for rb,re in zip(b['block_support'],e['block_support']):
    h.append('<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+esc(x)+'</td>' for x in [rb['folio'],rb['group'],f'{rb["known"]} / {rb["unknown"]}',f'{rb["ones"]} / {rb["known"]-rb["ones"]}',f'{re["known"]} / {re["unknown"]}',f'{re["ones"]} / {re["known"]-re["ones"]}'])+'</tr>')
h+=['</table></div><h2>Frozen application and complete results</h2><p>Aries (f70v1, f71r), Taurus (f71v, f72r1), Gemini (f72r2), and Cancer (f72r3): 120 slots in the exact synthetic geometry. Pisces remains excluded at 29 visible figures; Leo remains excluded because one fold location has uncertain presence. No fit-selected gaps were inserted.</p><p>The original scorer is unchanged: 18,424 distinct patterns representing 30,720 raw table/traversal/offset rules, both §457 and §458 included, 199 ring/group shifts with the full search repeated, and the two-feature correction retained. The input serialization, seeds and tie policy were frozen before scoring. Every raw traversal alias is retained with the complete candidate scores.</p><p><a href="APPLICATION.json">Application protocol</a> · <a href="APPLICATION-FREEZE.json">Pre-score freeze</a> · <a href="INPUT.json">Figure-level input and original annotation fields</a> · <a href="RESULTS.json">Results</a> · <a href="body-all-scores.json">All torso scores and aliases</a> · <a href="enclosure-all-scores.json">All enclosure scores and aliases</a> · <a href="run.py">Application code</a></p><p><a href="WINNING-RULES.json">Frozen empty winning set</a> · <a href="WINNER-FREEZE.json">Post-score freeze</a> · <a href="TOP-FITS.json">Nonqualifying diagnostics</a></p><h2>Ambiguities and exceptions</h2><p>The eligible inputs contain 21 unresolved torso classifications and five unresolved enclosure classifications; these counts can overlap. Star pigmentation remains unavailable, and candidate adjacent labels are not established ownership or scored text. The original eight-panel development inventory remains unchanged, including excluded Pisces and uncertain Leo.</p><p><a href="../zodiac-mapping-v84/report.html">Original image map and all development exceptions</a> · <a href="../zodiac-mapping-v84/ANNOTATIONS.json">Full unchanged inventory</a></p><details open><summary>Unresolved eligible figures</summary><table><tr><th>Figure</th><th>Torso</th><th>Enclosure</th><th>Original ambiguity note</th><th>Label association</th></tr>']
for r in data['records']:
    if r['body'] is None or r['enclosure'] is None:
        s=r['source']; h.append('<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+esc(v)+'</td>' for v in [r['figure_id'],s.get('body') or 'unresolved',s.get('enclosure') or 'unresolved',s.get('ambiguity',''),s.get('label_association','')])+'</tr>')
h+=['</table></details><h2>Held-out boundary</h2><p>Virgo, Libra, Scorpio and Sagittarius remain unannotated and unscored by this application. There is no qualifying rule to test on them. A future attempt would need independently established within-group visual information and its own qualification before any revised scoring—not resolution of ambiguities chosen to match these tables.</p></html>']
s='\n'.join(h); (P/'report.html').write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
class QA(HTMLParser):
    def handle_starttag(self,tag,attrs):
        for k,v in attrs:
            if k=='href': assert (P/v).exists(),v
QA().feed(s); assert s.count('<table')==s.count('</table>')
audit={'all_postscore_freeze_hashes_match':True,'html_parsed':True,'local_links_verified':True,'rendered_ui_checked':False,'heldout_scored':False,'both_features_zero_within_group_variation':True}
(P/'AUDIT.json').write_text(json.dumps(audit,indent=2),encoding='utf-8')
(P/'SHA256SUMS.json').write_text(json.dumps({p.name:hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest() for p in P.iterdir() if p.is_file() and p.name!='SHA256SUMS.json'},indent=2),encoding='utf-8')
print('Report complete; both features not estimable; frozen winning set empty; held-out signs unscored.')
